  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an integer NNN.\n\nYour task is to construct a matrix of size N×NN\\times NN×N satisfying all the following conditions:\n\n\nAll elements are between 111 and N2N^2N2;\nAll elements are pairwise **distinct**;\nThe sum of elements in every row is **odd**;\nThe sum of elements in every column is **odd**.\nIt can be shown that under the given constraints, at least one such matrix exists for every NNN.\n\nIf there are multiple answers, you may print any.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line of input containing a single integer, NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print NNN lines, each containing NNN integers.\n\nThe jthj^{th}jth integer of the ithi^{th}ith line must be the element in ithi^{th}ith row and jthj^{th}jth column of the matrix.\n\n\nIf there are multiple answers, you may print any one of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001\\leq T\\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤3001\\leq N\\leq 3001≤N≤300",
      "The sum of N2N^2N2 over all testcases does not exceed 10510^5105",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (49 points):** NNN is odd.",
      "**Subtask 2 (51 points):** NNN is even."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
